mod:param_redef_store_faces;
// 2026-11-16 (landing 177d2b9, row 2: DEF-685, seat D2's D5, stacked on row 1). A STORE THROUGH A POINTER PARAMETER THE CALLEE REDEFINED LANDS
// WHERE THE PARAMETER NOW POINTS, not in the argument first passed (`a = b; (<-a).lp = v`). The escape analysis walks a MARKED parameter's own
// chain (where the body pointed it) BESIDE main's record of the store at the parameter, never in its place, so the callee's summary records the
// store and the caller's view across the call is refused. A parameter is marked only on three roads: (1) it is assigned whole (`a = b`, in one
// branch too); (2) refs land on its own address ref (`rp = @r; <-rp = p2`); (3) `@o` or `$$ o`, under casts too, is handed to a callee whose
// summary stores refs through that parameter (`bothp(@o, o, p2, hq)`). An address taken alone (`rdhp(@p)`) marks nothing.
// One cell a face, its names suffixed with the cell's. Each face is accepted by main (acb78ea) and by row 1, and reads freed heap there (236 at
// -O0 and -O2 on roads 0-2, 97 under the detector; `t_pbr`, `t_pbrd`, `t_pbre` read it on road 0 only and run 67 on roads 1-2, the store being in
// one branch); each is refused here. The guards are in param_redef_store_guards.npk, the prices in param_redef_store_prices.npk, the right
// controls in tests/backend/programs/param_redef_store_ok.npk.
// THE FACES (56):
// D4's and seat D's cells (13): `t_pun`, `t_pbr`, `t_pmid`, `t_pbrd`, `t_pbre`, `t_pind`, `d4_bothpl`, `p_addr`, `p_call`, `p_loop`, `p_pon2`,
// `p_pun2`, `p_sl`.
// A4's r10 (4): `a4_fpar`, `a4_fpass`, `a4_fspp`, `a4_fswap`.
// A4's r13, `a4_fpp*` (3): `a4_fpp2`, `a4_fpp4`, `a4_fpp5`.
// A4's r14, the call road's routes `a4_q*` (8): `a4_qbm`, `a4_qdyn`, `a4_qgen`, `a4_qis`, `a4_qlater`, `a4_qmut`, `a4_qone`, `a4_qrec`.
// A4's r17, loops (4): `a4_flp`, `a4_flpb`, `a4_flpc`, `a4_flps`.
// A4's r18, setter roads (3): `a4_frfl`, `a4_frlc`, `a4_frsh`.
// A4's r21, a generic callee in another module (lib/param_redef_store_xlib.npk; with the same two cells inlined) (4): `a4_xmf`, `a4_xmg`,
// `a4_xmf_in`, `a4_xmg_in`.
// A4's r22 (1): `a4_qc4`.
// Seat D2's probes, `q_*` (11): `q_dir`, `q_opt`, `q_ppl`, `q_ret`, `q_stc`, `q_stf`, `q_tern`, `q_dad`, `q_dcast`, `q_gen`, `q_pon`.
// This row's probes (step 5): the address road under a no-root store, a pointer value handed through a parameter redefined twice, the one-hop
// no-root store, a pointer read through a redefined parameter (5): `k_nr6_r2`, `k_v_a`, `k_v_b`, `k_v19_r2`, `k_d17_r2`.
// Five cells main refuses already gain one site here and are named in the row's record, not here: `r1_pcp`, `t_pswap`, `a4_qfv`, `t_pwbr`,
// `t_pcalf_ok`.
use "./lib/param_redef_store_xlib.npk".*;
error:E5;
struct:K_t_pun = { int64:k; };
struct:H_t_pun = { List<int64>:l; int64:k; K_t_pun:kk; };
func:mk_t_pun = List<int64>() never fails { List<int64>:l = raw list_init::<int64>(1i64); drop list_push(@l, 1i64); pass l; };
func:mkh_t_pun = H_t_pun() never fails { pass H_t_pun{ l: raw mk_t_pun(), k: 2i64, kk: K_t_pun{ k: 3i64 } }; };
func:growh_t_pun = int64(H_t_pun->:w) never fails { loop(0i64, 64i64, 1i64) { drop list_push(@w.l, 1i64); } pass 7i64; };
func:growl_t_pun = int64(List<int64>->:l) never fails { loop(0i64, 64i64, 1i64) { drop list_push(l, 1i64); } pass 7i64; };
func:fp_t_pun = int64->(H_t_pun->:q) never fails { pass @((<-q).l[0i64]); };
func:idh_t_pun = H_t_pun->(H_t_pun->:q) never fails { pass q; };
func:getl_t_pun = List<int64>->(H_t_pun->:w) never fails { pass @w.l; };
struct:HPO_t_pun = { H_t_pun->:lp; List<int64>:own; };
struct:SQ_t_pun = { HPO_t_pun->:q; int64:z; };
struct:SR_t_pun = { SQ_t_pun->:sq; int64:z; };
